                  <msItem>
                     <title source="2012">Biblia</title>
                  <title source="5301">Biblia (at the end of a quire from the end of a copy of the Historia
                        scholastica, s. xiii in.)</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">Formerly Deen Park, Trustees of the late Mr G.
                        Brudenell, XVIII.B.3</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">Sotheby's 12.xii.1966, lot 220 to Maggs.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">Medieval binding (bare boards, bevelled). One
                        of two clasps remain.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">2 cols., 51 ll. </note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">Most of fol. 1 gone. 2nd leaf begins 'occisione
                        saul'.</note>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes" source="5301">Facs. of part of first leaf of Psalter in
                        Friends of the National Libraries Report for 1967, app., p. 10.</note>
                  </msItem>
