                        cathedral priory of St Cuthbert</orgName><p>"Liber sancti Cuthberti ..."
                        (sent to Stamford cell, q. v.).</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Formerly Deene Park, Trustees of the late Mr
                     G Brudenell, XVIII.B.3.</provenance>
               <provenance type="#e" source="5301"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_520">Stamford,
                        Lincolnshire. Benedictine priory of St Leonard; cell of Durham</orgName><p>'Liber sancti leonardi iuxta stanfo[...]'. 'Liber sancti
                        leonardi'.</p><p>'Liber sancti Cuthberti cuius vsus da[...] monasterio diui
                        leonardi iuxta stanfor[...] anno domni milesimo quingentesimo vice [...]'.
                        Also another similar inscription with date 'mo cccco xxijo [sic]'.</p><p>At
                        Stamford in s. xiv as appears from a pencil note on fol. 26r: 'ego Iohannes
                        de ho[...]a minor legi super hunc librum per totum annum apud stanfordeam
                        anno domini 1337 ...'.</p><p>(fol. 436v) 'prior sancti leona[...]'.</p><p>On
                        the 1st flyleaf, very much faded, is '[...] sancti leonardi et nostri
                        thom[... cr ...a...]'.</p><p>'[...]stat' quod magister Thomas accepit de
                        predicto priore libros infrascriptos</p><p>In primis liber sentenciarum 2o
                        folio dia pp[...] [?].</p><p>Item exposicio super epistolas pauli 2o folio
                        prophetabant</p><p>Item scriptum super primum sentenciarum 2o folio
                        quin</p><p>Item primam partem summe Thome' 2o folio
                     cognicio'.</p></provenance>
